<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $73.4 mln Sept 6.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $73.4 mln Sept 6.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $73.4 million deficit on September 6 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON SEPTEMBER 6</p>
<p>Exports: $131.9 million</p>
<p>Imports: $148.5 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $132.2 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $189 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $73.4 million</p>
<p>SEPTEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.042 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $707 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $555 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $909 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $19 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo Newsroom 55-11-2324411</p>
</text>
